Imports:
  - Types:
      - SManga
      - UpdateStrategy
    From: source-api/src/main/kotlin/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/source/model

Usages:
  chapter_flags_bitmask: |
    chapterFlags packs several independent tri-state/boolean display settings (sort direction,
    unread/downloaded/bookmarked filters, sort key, display mode) into one Long using disjoint
    bitmasks, each exposed as a derived read-only property that masks and compares against the
    relevant constant group.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the app's central domain aggregate: the manga entity itself, its cover-fetch
  projection, its partial-update counterpart, a duplicate-detection projection, and the
  three-way filter helper it and sibling library-filtering code use.

  Use `chapter_flags_bitmask` for Manga's derived filter/sort properties.
  Use `SManga` from Imports as the source-provided shape Manga is populated from.
  Use `UpdateStrategy` from Imports for Manga.updateStrategy.

---

"Manga(id: Long, source: Long, favorite: Boolean, lastUpdate: Long, nextUpdate: Long, fetchInterval: Int, dateAdded: Long, viewerFlags: Long, chapterFlags: Long, coverLastModified: Long, url: String, title: String, artist: String?, author: String?, description: String?, genre: List<String>?, status: Long, thumbnailUrl: String?, updateStrategy: UpdateStrategy, initialized: Boolean, lastModifiedAt: Long, favoriteModifiedAt: Long?, version: Long, notes: String, memo: JsonObject)":
  location: Manga.kt
  annotations: |
    The library's manga aggregate: source-provided metadata merged with the app's own
    library/tracking/display state. This is the single type every layer above the source
    boundary (data, domain interactors, presentation) works with.

    id: local database row id
    `source`: id of the owning Source/CatalogueSource
    `favorite`: whether this manga is currently in the user's library
    `lastUpdate`: epoch millis of the last successful chapter-list refresh
    nextUpdate: epoch millis this manga is next due for a background refresh
    `fetchInterval`: computed refresh interval in days, used to schedule nextUpdate
    `dateAdded`: epoch millis the manga was added to the library
    viewerFlags: packed reader-display settings, opaque outside the reader
    chapterFlags: packed chapter list sort/filter/display settings; see `chapter_flags_bitmask`
    url, `title`, `artist`, `author`, `description`, genre, status, `thumbnailUrl`: mirror
    the corresponding SManga fields
    updateStrategy: from Imports, see `UpdateStrategy`
    `initialized`: whether metadata has been fetched from the source at least once
    `version`, `lastModifiedAt`, `favoriteModifiedAt`: sync/conflict-resolution bookkeeping
    `notes`: free-form user notes
    memo: source-specific extra metadata carried over from SManga.memo

    Algorithm:
    1. expectedNextUpdate exposes nextUpdate as an Instant, or null once status is
       SManga.COMPLETED
    2. sorting/displayMode/unreadFilterRaw/downloadedFilterRaw/bookmarkedFilterRaw
       each mask chapterFlags against one constant group; unreadFilter/bookmarkedFilter
       further map the raw masked value to a TriState
    3. sortDescending() masks chapterFlags against the sort-direction bit

    Use `chapter_flags_bitmask`.
  properties:
    "expectedNextUpdate -> Instant?": |
      nextUpdate as an Instant, or null if the manga's status is completed.
    "sorting -> Long": |
      Chapter-list sort key extracted from chapterFlags.
    "displayMode -> Long": |
      Chapter-list display mode (by name or by number) extracted from chapterFlags.
    "unreadFilter -> TriState": |
      Library/chapter-list unread filter extracted from chapterFlags.
    "bookmarkedFilter -> TriState": |
      Library/chapter-list bookmarked filter extracted from chapterFlags.
  methods:
    "sortDescending() -> descending:Boolean": |
      Whether the chapter list sort direction bit in chapterFlags is set to descending.

"MangaCover(mangaId: Long, sourceId: Long, isMangaFavorite: Boolean, url: String?, lastModified: Long)":
  location: MangaCover.kt
  annotations: |
    Minimal projection of Manga carrying only what the cover-image loader needs, so cover
    fetching does not require the full aggregate. Built from a Manga via asMangaCover().

"MangaUpdate(id: Long, source: Long?, favorite: Boolean?, lastUpdate: Long?, nextUpdate: Long?, fetchInterval: Int?, dateAdded: Long?, viewerFlags: Long?, chapterFlags: Long?, coverLastModified: Long?, url: String?, title: String?, artist: String?, author: String?, description: String?, genre: List<String>?, status: Long?, thumbnailUrl: String?, updateStrategy: UpdateStrategy?, initialized: Boolean?, version: Long?, notes: String?, memo: JsonObject?)":
  location: MangaUpdate.kt
  annotations: |
    Sparse partial update for a Manga row: only non-null fields are written by the repository
    implementation. id is always required and identifies the target row. Built from a Manga
    via toMangaUpdate() as a starting point for a full-value update.

    Use `UpdateStrategy` from Imports for updateStrategy.

"MangaWithChapterCount(manga: Manga, chapterCount: Long)":
  location: MangaWithChapterCount.kt
  annotations: |
    A Manga paired with its known chapter count; used where a manga list needs the count
    without loading full chapter lists (e.g. duplicate-library-manga detection).

"applyFilter(filter: TriState, predicate: () -> Boolean) -> matches:Boolean":
  location: TriState.kt
  annotations: |
    Generic three-state filter evaluator shared by library/category filtering logic.

    `filter`: DISABLED always matches, ENABLED_IS matches when predicate() is true,
    ENABLED_NOT matches when predicate() is false
    `predicate`: the underlying boolean condition being filtered on
    `matches`: whether the item passes this filter

